  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkMagic.IncredibleAbilityGrowLife": "Hollicynthea seems to have an incredible ability to grow new life, and you're curious as to how that all works. Is she using some sort of magic?"
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkMagic.SmilesSlightMockery": "[pg]She smiles at you[if (hollidom) {, though there's a slight bit of mockery in her eyes| sweetly}]. [saystart][if (hollidom) {What, am I not good enough for you?|I'm afraid not, [name].}] It's not exactly my gift to give, so to speak. Perhaps if you were to already possess some ability yourself, I could guide you, but as it is... there is nothing I can do."
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkMarae.CantGoLike": "[pg][say:I can't very well go to her like this,] she says. [say:Being bound to this tree does have its limits. I suppose I would indeed like to meet Mother, though she's a bit... 'temperamental', these days.]"
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkMarae.FirstCameGiftMarae": "When Holli first came to you, she mentioned how she was a gift from Marae, but does she even know her mother?"
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkMarae.HowKnowGoddessFirst": "[pg]How did she know the goddess's will in the first place, then? Can she communicate with her in some way?"
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkMarae.JoltSuddenContactTendril": "[pg]You jolt at a sudden contact, and look down to see a teasing tendril snaking its way up your side."
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkMarae.JustCloserLovelyStart": "[pg][say:Just getting a bit closer would be a lovely start, though...]"
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkMarae.SmilesDaughterLinked": "[pg]She smiles. [say:Hmm... Yes. We can communicate, in a sense. I am her daughter, linked to her by birth. Mother Marae is the world itself, the wellspring of everything, and even turned, her tendrils run deep. I am but a bud on a branch, but far more lies below. If you knew the full consequences of your actions...] Her expression grows sweet, almost saccharine, and you find yourself oddly unnerved. [say:Well, you would never want to leave the comfort of my side,] she finishes, her voice heavy with sensuality."
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkMenu.WhatSubjectDemonDryad": "What subject do you bring up with the demonic dryad?"
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkReproduction.LaughsSurprisingGaiety": "[pg]Holli just laughs with surprising gaiety, covering her mouth with a hand. Seems you won't be getting any more details than that..."
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkReproduction.LeavesLotQuestionsUnanswered": "[pg]Well, that still leaves a lot of questions unanswered. How quickly do they grow? What exactly does the process entail? How many can she have at once? Does she enjoy \"bearing\" them?"
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkReproduction.PersistentJuicesNotGrasp": "Holli's been very persistent about getting your \"juices\", but {0}. Does she really not get pregnant?"
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkReproduction.RespondsLivelyGlint": "[pg][say:Yes, I do,] she responds, a lively glint in her eyes. You wait for a few moments, but her expression makes it clear that she's either unwilling or unable to answer the other questions. Still... there's one niggling thought left at the back of your mind. Aren't they technically your children?"
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkReproduction.SighsCannotBreedWant": "[pg]She sighs. [say:No, [name], I cannot breed in the way you might want,] she says, though you don't know if it's disappointment or annoyance on her face. [say:I am unakin to you. All I offer is my bounty, and if it is not to your pleasing, then [if (hollidom) {that is your issue|I would be happy to please you in other ways}].]"
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkReproduction.SmirksReachesStrokesBranch": "[pg]She smirks. [say:Has it not?] She reaches up and lovingly strokes {0}one of her branches. [say:Your libations go to good use--they nourish me, grow my strength, and{1} allow me to bear you fruit. They are my offerings, the Goddess's gift to you.]"
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkRooted.EyebrowsArchDoesntKnow": "[pg][say:Hm?] Her eyebrows arch, and it seems possible that she actually doesn't know what you mean. Does she really never feel bad about not being able to move? About not being able to talk to anyone outside of your camp? About being cut off from the world?"
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkRooted.InResponseSimplyGiggles": "[pg]In response, the demonic dryad simply giggles. [say:No, not at all. [if (hollidom) {If I was displeased, I would make that known|I wouldn't dream of leaving you}].] She turns to the side, seeming to examine a stray branch of her tree. She doesn't seem interested in elaborating, but you're still curious, so you ask again, this time more specifically about her feelings on the matter."
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkRooted.LivedWholeLifeSpot": "She's lived her whole life--short as that time may be--right here in this one spot. You can't really relate, but you imagine that someone in her position might get lonely or yearn for escape. Does she?"
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkRooted.SniffsEarthNotOff": "[pg][say:Ah. No, I don't feel bad about that, as I'm not cut off from anything.] She sniffs. [say:[if (hollidom) {It's even somewhat amusing hearing that from you--it's much the other way around. Can [i:you] feel the earth around you? Do [i:you] branch out, your fingers slipping unseen over the land?|Don't worry about me, I'm quite connected. Connected to the earth, connected to Marae, connected to [i:you], whenever possible.}]] She gives a playful smirk. [say:Believe me, [name], I am not lonely, though that doesn't mean I wouldn't appreciate your 'company'.]"
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkSeeds.AlwaysTossedCoresAway": "You realize that you've always just tossed the cores away after you're done eating Holli's fruits, but those cores have seeds in them. Furthermore, the very fact that she produces fruit would suggest that she's spreading herself in some way, but aside from the general vegetation she grows around your camp, you haven't seen anything that even comes close to her or her tree."
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkSeeds.DodgingQuestionFirmAnswer": "[pg]Seems to you like she's dodging the question. You shake your head and ask for a firm answer--what happens with the seeds?"
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkSeeds.NoticesConcernNotWorry": "[pg]The dryad seems to notice a hint of concern in your voice, replying, [say:Do not worry, Champion, you are nourishing the land.] There's [if (hollidom) {a hint of mockery|a soothing serenity}] in her voice as she speaks, [if (hollidom) {but|and}] you find yourself slowly succumbing to its cloying effect. [say:Your efforts are not wasted, you can be sure. You are a worthy recipient of Mother's benevolence.]"
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkSeeds.PoutsEyesDontWorry": "[pg]Holli pouts her lips and bats her eyes. [say:Don't worry, [name], don't you worry about anything. Come here, I will comfort you.] Her arms extend out to either side, and she gives you a warm smile."
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkSeeds.SmilesReturnEarthStrength": "[pg]Hollicynthea smiles. [say:They return to the earth, your strength added to theirs. Our Great Mother accepts all offerings. She is the land, and everything that walks upon it is hers. Oh, but I think you wanted something more specific than that. Hm. I believe there is a saying among mortals, 'A man only begins to grasp the true meaning of life when he plants a tree under whose shade he knows he will never sit.' Something to that effect.]"
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkSeeds.WhatMeanHeartTightens": "[pg][if (cor < 66) {Your heart suddenly tightens, and your breathing quickens just a bit|Some distant premonition of ill tidings rests in your heart}]. What does she mean?"
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkSeedsEmbrace.LetBreathPeaceComfort": "You let out a breath, and your body feels at peace. The dryad's arms look like the most comfortable place in the world right now, so you s[if (singleleg) {l|tr}]ide forward and meet them. She lets out a breathy purr as her skin contacts [if (hasplainskin) {yours|your [skindesc]}], and you can't hold back a similar sign of contentment."
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkSeedsEmbrace.RatherTireWarmthSt": "[pg]But rather than tire you, you find that the warmth of her embrace is actually quite stimulating. Your face begins to grow hot as blood rushes to your loins, anticipation starting to tickle your nerves even before her vines snake up your sides to caress your body. You feel a pair of hands on your chin which guide your gaze up, up, up to meet hers."
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkSeedsEmbrace.SwirlingBlackPitsEnrapture": "[pg]Those swirling black pits enrapture you. [say:[if (hollidom) {Share in my bounty|Please let me pleasure you}], [name]. Give me your seed.] You briefly wonder if you would be able to deny this request, if even a single part of you wanted to."
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkSeedsReject.RetreatHolliCallOut": "[pg]As you retreat from her tree, you hear Holli call out from behind you. [say:[if (hollidom) {You will return to me, [name]. You cannot resist.|Please, [name]! Come here, and let me make it all better!}]"
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkSeedsReject.ShutBestNotThink": "[pg]You shut your ears as best you can and try not to think about anything. Maybe if you try hard enough, you'll be able to forget all of this entirely."
  "Scenes.Holliscene.HolliTalkSeedsReject.TearAwayStumbleBack": "You tear your eyes away and stumble back. You don't know exactly what you've done, [if (cor < 66) {and maybe you don't even|but you don't really}] care--you just have to get away from her right now, seeds be damned."
  "Scenes.Holliscene.JojoTransformAndRollOut.BlurtsUnbelievableSayStart": "[pg][say: Unbelievable...] he blurts. [saystart]"
  "Scenes.Holliscene.JojoTransformAndRollOut.ComeHerePlease": "[say: [name], come here please.]"
  "Scenes.Holliscene.JojoTransformAndRollOut.EvenKnowingFornicateName": "And even knowing that this could be the case, you still chose to fornicate with it? [name]... I cannot say that I am not disappointed. This place is not safe for me anymore. For now, I will return to the forest."
  "Scenes.Holliscene.JojoTransformAndRollOut.GesturesHummingVerdantGrown": "[pg][say: That plant you were... engaged with earlier seems to have grown.] He gestures toward the humming, verdant woman, currently peeking from her tree boldly. [say: I was going to encourage you to rid your campsite of such an abomination, but one of the things it keeps repeating to itself gave me pause. It seems to believe it is a child of Marae - though anyone with eyes to see can tell that it's a demon.]"
  "Scenes.Holliscene.JojoTransformAndRollOut.GesturesStrangePortalSite": "[pg][say: Perhaps it had escaped your notice until now, but the portal site has a somewhat out-of-place... guest. That tree actually contains a creature.] He gestures toward the strange plant. [say: I overheard it speaking to itself. It seems to believe that it has been put here by Marae, but such a thing... Anyone looking at that monster can see that it is a demon, not the kindred of a goddess.]"
  "Scenes.Holliscene.JojoTransformAndRollOut.JojoCallingBorderPolitely": "[pg]Jojo is calling to you from the border of the camp. Politely, you approach the monk. This is probably the first time since your rather violent initial meeting that he's addressed you so directly, and you're a bit curious as to why."
  "Scenes.Holliscene.JojoTransformAndRollOut.JojoNoCompanionBold": "[pg](<b>Jojo is no longer a companion!</b>)"
  "Scenes.Holliscene.JojoTransformAndRollOut.LooksArgumentResignedShake": "Jojo looks at you sadly; any argument you try to make is met with a resigned shake of his head. [saystart]If the creature truly is the demonic offspring of a corrupted earth spirit, doubtless it will be powerful and the wrath of its parent severe."
  "Scenes.Holliscene.JojoTransformAndRollOut.MakesPoliteForestAssistance": "[say: Until then, you will find me in the forest if you need my assistance.] Jojo makes a polite bow and departs."
  "Scenes.Holliscene.JojoTransformAndRollOut.MonkWidenSurpriseSumrise": " The monk's eyes widen in surprise and surmise."
  "Scenes.Holliscene.JojoTransformAndRollOut.MortalResourcesDestroyEscape": " Though, a mortal of your stature and resources may be able to destroy her and escape the reprisal. I would counsel against direct confrontation until you are sure of victory, but if you must fight, then call upon me and you will have what aid I can give."
  "Scenes.Holliscene.JojoTransformAndRollOut.NonethelessPositionConfront": " Nonetheless, if you find yourself in a position where you must confront this demon or perish, call upon me. I will render what aid I can, though I prefer it not be in vain."
  "Scenes.Holliscene.JojoTransformAndRollOut.NotWillingAdmitChanged": "Not willing to lie to your friend, you also admit that she seems to have changed after your actions in the factory - that, though you were trying to render the tanks permanently inoperable, the spillage you created pushed the chthonic spirit over the edge."
  "Scenes.Holliscene.JojoTransformAndRollOut.QuietlyInterruptNewsMarae": "[pg]Quietly, you interrupt to break the bad news to Jojo; that you found Marae recently, quite corrupted and soulless, and that the growth in your camp does seem to be an offshoot of the now-twisted tree. "
  "Scenes.Holliscene.JojoTransformAndRollOut.SayEndAgain": "[sayend]"
  "Scenes.Holliscene.JojoTransformAndRollOut.SoSayingPressesTalisman": "[sayend] So saying, he presses a small talisman into your hand."
  "Scenes.Holliscene.JojoTransformAndRollOut.ThoughLeaveNeedlessDetails": "Though, you do leave out the precise, needless details of what caused the change."
  "Scenes.Holliscene.JojoTransformAndRollOut.ToThinkConsiderEnemy": "To think that I must now consider Marae herself my enemy. Forgive me, but this place is not safe for us anymore if it has attracted the attention of such a creature. For now, I will return to the forest. I know that you believe your mission keeps you here, but I urge you to stay away from that thing and watch the portal from an adequate distance."
  "Scenes.Holliscene.LetZeFuckingSproutLive.PlantAddedItemsBold": "[pg](<b>'Plant' added to your items menu</b>. It's too small to know what it will grow into yet. You can currently remove it at your leisure.)"
  "Scenes.Holliscene.LetZeFuckingSproutLive.StayCorruptHasntDone": "Looking down at the sapling, you stay your wrath. It may be corrupt, but it hasn't done anything to harm you just yet. You give it a little pat on the uppermost leaves and leave it be. It's not like it's going anywhere."
  "Scenes.Holliscene.Level4RideHollisTentacruels.AnHourLaterBold": "[pg]<b>An hour later...</b>"
